From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P80 builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Teclast P80: leave out AudioFX, SecureElement, TeleService
 and ONS

AudioFX, SecureElement and TeleService run as persistent processes from
boot, even when disabled with `pm disable` (measured on LineageOS 24.0:
~6 MB PSS each for the first two). The tablet has no secure element, NFC
or eSIM for com.android.se to serve, and LineageOS's equalizer (AudioFX)
is optional: audio works without it. TeleService (com.android.phone,
~16 MB PSS, persistent) returns from PhoneGlobals.onCreate() right away
when FEATURE_TELEPHONY is missing, as on this Wi-Fi-only tablet, so it
registers no service and the framework already runs without its
services here.

ONS (com.android.ons, the opportunistic network service for devices
with SIM cards, persistent) has to go with TeleService: it shares the
android.uid.phone user and the com.android.phone process, and its
manifest requests only RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED and READ_PHONE_STATE.
ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE came from TeleService's manifest, so without
TeleService ONS crash-looped at boot (SecurityException from
ConnectivityService in ONSProfileActivator, ~180 restarts a minute,
~30 % CPU at idle; measured on the tablet with only TeleService left
out).
---
diff --git a/overrides/Android.mk b/overrides/Android.mk
--- a/overrides/Android.mk
+++ b/overrides/Android.mk
@@ -84,7 +84,11 @@
 	messaging \
 	Stk \
 	ImsServiceEntitlement \
-	QuickAccessWallet
+	QuickAccessWallet \
+	AudioFX \
+	SecureElement \
+	TeleService \
+	ONS
 LOCAL_MODULE_TAGS := optional
 LOCAL_MODULE_CLASS := ETC
 LOCAL_MODULE_PATH := $(TARGET_OUT_ETC)
